\newlabel{tab:factorial}{{1}{4}{The complete $2^3$ factorial over nine problems, pooled over two independent replicates (120 verified samples per run). frac = fraction of the seed-to-record gap closed. E has the best mean and is best or tied-best in five of nine problems; D alone is bimodal: best on wide valid manifolds (pmfs, sequences), catastrophic where validity is fragile (packing geometry, constrained integer sets); BD is the only arm that never collapses, CD the one that collapses most; two problems (isosceles-free, $180!$) are family plateaus where every arm meets the same wall.\relax }{table.caption.7}{}}
