\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The completed $2^3$ at a glance (cell means over nine problems, two replicates). Memory-on cells (blue) hold the four best gap fractions; D-on cells (circles) hold the highest construction-hash diversity; the two axes barely interact ($\beta _{M\times R} \approx 0$). Collapse counts in parentheses: memory+repulsion is the only arm that never collapses; agenda+repulsion collapses most.\relax }}{6}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cube}{{2}{6}{The completed $2^3$ at a glance (cell means over nine problems, two replicates). Memory-on cells (blue) hold the four best gap fractions; D-on cells (circles) hold the highest construction-hash diversity; the two axes barely interact ($\beta _{M\times R} \approx 0$). Collapse counts in parentheses: memory+repulsion is the only arm that never collapses; agenda+repulsion collapses most.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
